# Google Calendar sync. There are two ways to connect; pick ONE. See docs/GOOGLE_SETUP.md.
# Copy this file to .env and never commit .env.

# --- Option A (recommended): a service account writing into a calendar you own.
# No consent screen, and no credential that expires. You create a calendar in Google Calendar,
# share it with the service account's email ("Make changes to events"), and paste its ID here.
# The key itself is a FILE, not a variable: .data/google-service-account.json (gitignored).
CALENDAR_ID=

# --- Option B: OAuth, where the planner creates and owns its own calendar.
# Needs a "Desktop app" OAuth client and `npm run auth`. While the Cloud app is in Testing mode
# Google expires the refresh token after 7 days, so this needs re-running weekly.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
